<title>USA: Hughes Electronics secures contract.</title>
<headline>Hughes Electronics secures contract.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hughes Electronics Corp unit Hughes Data Systems said Tuesday it has secured a contract worth up to $171 million from the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office to provide desktop workstations, monitors, printers and related items.</p>
<p>Hughes said the one-year fixed-price contract is worth some $152 million, with a potential maximum value of $171 million. The contract has two one-year options.</p>
<p>The award is the third major contract win of the year for Hughes Data Systems, the company said.</p>
</text>
